Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: wrong8007-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: kmod, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: wrong8007-utils
Description: programmable kernel-resident dead man's switch for last-resort execution
 Wrong Boot carries out a decision you made in advance by following the
 instructions you left the moment the kernel sees a condition you define.
 Keyboard, USB and network triggers come built in and new triggers plug
 into the same core.
 .
 This package provides the module source for DKMS, the wrong8007-params
 parameter check and the wrong8007 systemd service.

Package: wrong8007-utils
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: userspace control and heartbeat utilities for wrong8007
 This package provides wrong8007ctl. It sends heartbeats and test traffic
 to a machine running Wrong Boot.
